<title>ITALY: Ciampi sees tiny H2 CPI rise, no demand pressure.</title>
<headline>Ciampi sees tiny H2 CPI rise, no demand pressure.</headline>
<dateline>MILAN 1997-06-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Italian Treasury Minister Carlo Azeglio Ciampi said the government expected a light rise in inflation in the second half of 1997 but &quot;more of a statistical nature than of a substantial nature&quot;.</p>
<p>&quot;For the future I don't see inflation stimuli from demand,&quot; he told Il Sole financial daily in an interview.</p>
</text>
